---
title: Coffee Balls
description: Pecan butter cookies with a teaspoon of instant coffee in the dough, rolled in confectioners' sugar.
tags: [cookies, baking, mimi]
course: dessert
icons: [cookie, coffee-beans, butter]
difficulty: easy
yield: 36%cookies
---

Cream the @butter{227%g}(1 cup) and @sugar{66%g}(1/3 cup). Add the @cold water{2%tsp}, @instant coffee{1%tsp}, and @vanilla{2%tsp}, mixing well after each addition.

Blend in the @all-purpose flour{2%cup} and @pecans{113%g}(1 cup, chopped, or walnuts). Chill for ~chill{4%hours} or overnight.

Shape into balls and bake on an ungreased #cookie sheet{} at 325°F (165°C) for about ~bake{18-20%minutes}.

Remove from the pan and cool slightly, then roll in @confectioners' sugar{}.
